# Module: my_pitches_modal
Compile unit for the Forum Frontend.
Generates: `frontend/src/components/my_pitches_modal.tsx` (current hand-authored code is the reference output)

## Behavior
- Author-only dialog opened from the masthead "🔒 My pitches" control; labeled "Only you can see these."
- Lists the caller's pending pitches from `api_client.getMyFeatures` (`GET /api/features/mine`): `screening` state shows the pulsing "🛡️ Guardagent is screening your pitch..." row; `rejected` shows reason-mapped copy, one line per `reason` category (never a generic fallback) — `security` → "Your pitch didn't clear screening — rephrase and try again."; `off_topic` → "Great idea, but it's outside what this app is about — check the Sandbox to see what we're building."; `unclear` → "Your title and description seemed to describe different things — try again with them lined up."; `already_shipped` → "Looks like this already shipped in {shipped_version} — check it out in the Sandbox!" (interpolate `shipped_version`) — each with a Dismiss action.
- Rejected entries also vanish automatically when their 72h TTL lapses server-side — treat a disappeared entry as dismissed, not an error.
- Promotion: when a pending pitch's `feature_requests` INSERT arrives via Realtime (matched by `feature_id`), remove it here and celebrate as it enters the public feed.
- Friendly empty state inviting a first pitch. **Never render any of this inline with the public feed.**

